rtf_details:
{"ops":[{"insert":"Curious about amateur radio, and how you can get involved?

Winter Field day, "...aims to help participants improve their preparedness for disasters and enhance their operational abilities in adverse conditions." according to the Winter Field Day Assn. Furthermore, to "encourage a diverse range of activities, including the use of non-commercial power sources, the deployment of multiple antennas, establishing satellite contacts, and more."
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be operating from 11 am until 4 pm on Saturday, January 25, 2025, on Phone and CW using the club callsign W8DGN and 4O OH. We will set up at 10 am at the Twin Oak Shelter in the Hills and Dales MetroPark at 2655 S Patterson Blvd. in Kettering, OH.

All are invited!
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Ridge ARC will hold Winter Field Day at a Cabin on Lake Murray (1350 Shore Rd, Gilbert, SC). There is space to set up 2 or 3 stations inside the cabin and plenty of space to set up a table station (BYOT) on the porch or in the yard. There is also space for 3 or 4 campers. We already have a couple scheduled, so if you want to bring out a camper, please reach out ASAP. There are a couple beds inside and space for camping tents outside. Please contact W1MRC@Outlook.com with any questions. Visitors are encouraged to attend. We plan to arrive around 0900 on Saturday. Check our website for updates closer to January. 

Talk-In 147.255+ 123.0 & 146.550 Simplex
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"KB6Q, KN6MLT, KG6B, N3BEN

3 site weekend campout. 
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Multiple HF stations operating 24/7 for the event.

Satellite contacts on 2m and 70cm. We have built an automatic tracking ground station antenna array for this event.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"For the first time with our new club call sign "},{"attributes":{"bold":true},"insert":"Kilo Whiskey Four Red Oaks"},{"insert":", but as our fifth year in WFD, the Red Oaks group will be on the air!

We will be located at the same site at the Red Oaks RV Resort in Bushnell FL, on SW 20th Drive. Look on APRS for KW4RO at "},{"attributes":{"link":"https://aprs.fi/#!call=a%2FKW4RO"},"insert":"aprs.fi"},{"insert":"
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The St. Louis QRP Society will be operating from Stacy Park in Olivette, MO using N0A.  We plan to have 3 CW stations on the air and one multi-mode (SBB & Digital).

73 de WB0TUA
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Will be operating as N3Y at the Dover Motor Speedway parking area, 287 Moor Farm Ln, Dover, off of Persimmon Tree Ln.  We plan to operate for the full 24 hours and begin set up on Friday afternoon..  We will have two structures, one motor home and one cargo trailer.  Plenty of parking.  

For information, contact Paul, N3BUH, at "},{"attributes":{"color":"#5e5e5e"},"insert":"paultuley@live.com of Jerry, N3KRX, at n3krx@aol.com or at 302-359-1121.  Talk-in on the 146.910 (-)(77 HZ PL) KCARC repeater."},{"insert":"
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be located at the Oklahoma City Office of Emergency Management, utilizing the field outside, along with some mobile trailers in the parking lot.  We will be operational for the entire 30-hour event. Come and go as you would like; no advanced notice is required, and our volunteers will be here around the clock. 

We are located at 4600 N Martin Luther King Blvd. From of MLK Blvd, you will turn east on Meyers Ave, and on the south side of the road is our facility. You will see trailers and tents setup. Go to gate #2 and there is a call box, you can push the call button and we will open the gate for you. 
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The 146.985 [W3GMS] Repeater Group welcomes the public and all radio operators to join us for Winter Field Day. Our WFD QTH will be at Lines Self Storage, 964 Pottstown Pike, Chester Springs, PA 19425. For information, contact WA3VEE at wa3vee@arrl.net

Ham Radio is alive and well! Come see what we are doing and get on the air!


"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The outdoor 3 day campout will be set-up on Friday at 9am, January 24th at the "},{"attributes":{"link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/3Q9sBaeevV4aBiX18"},"insert":"Georgetown California Airport"},{"insert":" Campground. We will be operating through the event close with three stations on 23cm - 160m, phone, cw and digital modes. Also will attempt a satellite FM and a SSB/CW contact.

Event updates will be posted on Facebook.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be operating out of the Massie Township Fire Department, located at 10 Harveysburg Rd, Harveysburg OH 45032 from 11am to 11pm on Saturday "},{"attributes":{"background":"transparent","color":"#000000"},"insert":"January 25, 2025"},{"insert":".

Warren County AuxComm will have amateur radio examinations starting at 2:00pm, https://larc-vec.org/displaysession.php?session=13359

"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"This is a small activation for WFD where we will be working with our club and other local interested hams.

OPEN TO ALL - FEEL FREE TO STOP BY
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Meeting in the parking lot of Lonestar Premier Productions. 

Talk-In frequency is 146.420 simplex.  Use a tone of 123.0 to come out through the hub.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"For the first time, our club has decided to take part in the Winter Field Day.  As a club we have held many Field Day events and have had several visitors.  We would like to welcome all to come and visit us at the Fort Johnson Fire House #2 on Saturday January 25, 2025.  We plan on being at the location at 11:00 am EST for the day.

For more Information, please email us at info@efmarc.org.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Kg4Vet & kJ4uLz will be operating from Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway Park Working on Pota Kilo join us for a fun Experience also live streaming on Youtube "},{"attributes":{"header":1},"insert":"
"},{"insert":"http://www.youtube.com/@PotaPower01-m2b

"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Site is open to public 11:00 A.M. to 5:00 P.M. on Saturday. 

Get your Amateur Radio Licenses or upgrade with us during WFD!!! hamstudy.org/sessions/kg4ogc
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Bellbrook Amateur Radio Club will be deploying for Winter Field Day 2025 to the Twin Oaks Shelter at the Hills and Dales Metropark at 2655 S. Patterson Blvd., Kettering, OH 45409. We will begin setting up at 10 am on Saturday, January 25th, and operate from 11 am until about 5 pm under the club callsign, W8DGN. There will be hot food, coffee, water, and sodas available. The shelter has a fireplace but is otherwise open.

The public is invited and welcome!
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"FARA plans on 4M/VA, sadly no VE Session this year. 

Visitors PLEASE email fieldday@w4va.org to coordinate your times, we are very welcoming and want you to have the best experience but due to  our location weather may impact our ability to host, so pre-arranging visitation is strongly advised in order to make certain that we have the facilities and the staffing to give you the best experience possible.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be operating for Saturday only. Visitors welcome. We plan to have 2 radios setup outside using portable power. We intend to have a Satellite station and possibly a microwave station setup for demonstration.
Location is the Salvation Army parking lot at 10725 Alta St. Grass Valley, Ca.

"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Princeton Ham Radio Club will once again participate in Winter Field Day activities for 2025.  This year we will operate out of the EOC and Mobile EOC during the event.  We will be simulating a time where we would need to work interoperable with other entities.

The public is invited to come share in the activities.  We will be at 102 Northfield Drive in Princeton, KY in the rear of the Ambulance Bay.  Please reach out for more information to 270-963-1516 or w4kbl.org@gmail.com
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Miami County Amateur Radio club invites all amateurs in the area, or anyone interested in ham radio to join us for Winter Field Day 2025! 

Please bring food, snacks, or drinks! The club will provide a meat and cheese tray.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"My current plan is to operate in the southeast corner of Chuck Heinrich Memorial Park, in El Paso, Texas.  This will not be a 24-hour operation.  I will set up at some time, operate for as long as I'm comfortable, but then shut down and go home.  When I go home, I will cease my operation, so as not to confuse the category.
73/ W9CSM

"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Travelers Rest Amateur Radio Club will operate two stations under emergency conditions, using temporary antennas, batteries, solar power, and portable generators. The Club will initially operate from it's Ham Shack located near the Fire Station and will also operate from the Snack Shack Pavilion. Our goal is to test our equipment, expand our skills, demonstrate amateur radio to the Travelers Rest community and talk to as many other Winter Field Day ham stations as we can throughout the United States, Canada, Mexico and elsewhere.

Talk-in will be on 146.430 MHz simplex, PL 100 Hz.   
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will have two communications trailers setup at the Marion TWP Vol. Fire Dept location in Hocking County. This site is visible from the county road and is 5.6 miles from the intersection of SR 664 and Hunter in Logan. Open to the public. 

30737 Logan Horns Mill Rd, Logan, OH 43138
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Sagamore Hill Historic Site was the home of President Theodore Roosevelt and POTA location US-0856. 

I will be operating portable with a few field deployable antennas such as a 53’ Rybakov and tactical delta loop. 
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"St. Lucie County ARES will be holding a Winter Field Day event on Saturday, January 25 at Museum Pointe Park, 414 NW Seaway Dr., Ft. Pierce, FL. All operations will be on generator power. Solar power is also possible.

Adjacent to the Saint Lucie Historical Society, the public is invited to participate.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be operating from the Cumberland County EMA auxiliary communications trailer next to the field to the left of the Cumberland County Regional Communications Center parking lot, at 22 High Street, Windham, ME.

Setup begins at 10 AM Saturday, operating from 11 AM Saturday to 5 PM Sunday, Eastern Time. Attendees may warm up and enjoy some potluck food in the EMA bunker.
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will meet in the lower level of the visitors center around 9am on January 25th and will operate until we decide to shut things down for the day or near dark at the latest.  Come on down and have some fun with the group and get on the air.  We will be operating using battery power. 

If you have any questions just email them to OCARCIndiana@gmail.com
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"Out at Lake Mead at the Las Vegas Bay Campground.  I will arrive early Saturday and campout till Sunday afternoon

36.128956, -114.873611
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"We will be operating from the Elmhurst Fire Department Training tower, inside the training room.

901 N Addison Street – Elmhurst, located behind the McDonald's!
"}]}

{"ops":[{"insert":"The Everglades Amateur Radio Club will be participating in the annual Winter Field day activities. Everyone is welcome to join us. This is sure to be a great time to have fun with radio, learn and just have a good time with new and old friends.

Joins us Jan Dec 25th at the "},{"attributes":{"link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/3zitJxmvKyJ6569Z7"},"insert":"Homestead Bay Front Park"},{"insert":".  We will be there early morning and staying the night.
"}]}
